 A Vancouver police officer recently commended for his part in a water rescue just went beyond the call of duty yet again, this time jumping into frigid waters to save a stranded dog That's when Const Jason Doucette Police said it was a ball the dog chased, not a bird as reported by a Twitter user who took pictures On Sunday, police identified the officer as Peter Colenutt Others show him in bare feet and a short-sleeved shirt making his way across the snow-covered ground back to a squad car These weather conditions & temp of water is a risk for anyone Thank U Peter...over & above 👍 — @ShayMoyer 

