 Photo: Thomas Cordy Image 1 of / 13 Caption Close Image 1 of 13 FILE- In this Oct. 12, 2011, file photo, Anastasia, left, and Alexandria Duval, known as Alison and Ann Dadow before they changed their names, stand in the window of their yoga studio in West Palm Beach, Fla The arrest comes after the Maui Police Department issued a warrant for Alexandria Duval's arrest when a grand jury indicted her on a second-degree murder charge She's accused of killed her twin sister, Anastasia, after their vehicle plunged off a Hawaii cliff in May 2016 (Skip Dickstein/Times Union) Image 10 of 13 Image 11 of 13 Alexandria Duval aka Alison Dadow appears in Albany County Court before Judge William Carter on Friday, Nov. 18, 2016 Duval was injured in the crash Kindlon, from the Public Defender's Office, said she will not waive her right to an extradition hearing On May 29, the women's SUV plunged off a 200-foot cliff on Maui's rocky shore during what was described as a hair-pulling fight over the steering wheel, the Associated Press reports Kindlon described the crash as an accident The sisters were originally from the Utica area, according to the Star Advertiser of Honolulu
